    "question": "Cristobal read 15 more than three times the pages that Beatrix read. If Beatrix read 704 pages, how many more pages did Cristobal read?",
    "gold": "1423",
    "answer": "Cristobal read: 15 + 3 * 704 = <<15+3*704=2127>>2127 pages\n2127 - 704 = <<2127-704=1423>>1423 pages\nCristobal read 1423 more pages than Beatrix.\n#### 1423"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many more pages Cristobal read compared to Beatrix, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the number of pages Beatrix read.\n2. Use the information that Cristobal read 15 more than three times the pages that Beatrix read.\n3. Calculate the number of pages Cristobal read.\n4. Find the difference between the number of pages Cristobal read and the number of pages Beatrix read.\n\nLet's start with the number of pages Beatrix read. According to the problem, Beatrix read 704 pages.\n\nNext, we calculate the number of pages Cristobal read. The problem states that Cristobal read 15 more than three times the pages that Beatrix read. We can express this mathematically as:\n\\[ \\text{Number of pages Cristobal read} = 3 \\times \\text{Number of pages Beatrix read} + 15 \\]\nSubstituting the number of pages Beatrix read into the equation, we get:\n\\[ \\text{Number of pages Cristobal read} = 3 \\times 704 + 15 \\]\nNow, we perform the multiplication and addition:\n\\[ 3 \\times 704 = 2112 \\]\n\\[ 2112 + 15 = 2127 \\]\nSo, Cristobal read 2127 pages.\n\nTo find out how many more pages Cristobal read compared to Beatrix, we subtract the number of pages Beatrix read from the number of pages Cristobal read:\n\\[ 2127 - 704 = 1423 \\]\n\nTherefore, Cristobal read \\(\\boxed{1423}\\) more pages than Beatrix.",
